<p class="text-center fw-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">JOBLINK TERMS &amp; CONDITIONS</p>
<p class="text-center mb-4">Pangasinan State University &ndash; Alaminos City Campus</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">1. What JobLink Is</h2>
<p>JobLink is the career-placement platform for PSU Alaminos City students, alumni, partner companies, and Job Coordinator staff. It connects job seekers with employers and supports the university's tracer study and job-placement reporting.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">2. Account Eligibility</h2>
<p>Student and Alumni accounts are activated using a Student ID on file with your Job Coordinator. Company and Job Coordinator accounts are provisioned by authorized university staff. You may not create or use an account using another person's identity or credentials.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">3. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>To use JobLink, we collect information such as your name, date of birth, gender, civil status, nationality, course/program, year level or year graduated, contact details including email and mobile number, home address, and, if you choose to add one, a profile picture.</p>
<p>Students and alumni applying to jobs send the company a copy of their JobLink CV, together with their name, course and year, email, mobile number, and city and province. The copy does not include your date of birth, gender, civil status or street address. Clearances are handled separately, as described in section 5.</p>
<p>This information is used to verify your identity, match you with relevant opportunities, and support PSU's official tracer study reporting to partner employers and accrediting bodies.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">4. Searchable Profiles (Your Choice)</h2>
<p>By default, only a company you apply to can see your CV. Agreeing to these Terms &amp; Conditions does not make your profile searchable.</p>
<p>In Profile settings you may choose &ldquo;Make my profile searchable by partner companies&rdquo;. If you do, partner companies can find your CV when they search, even if you have not applied to them. They can see your name, course and year, city and province, and your CV. They cannot see your email, mobile number or LinkedIn and portfolio links; a company gets those only when you apply to one of its jobs. They never see your street address, date of birth, gender, civil status or profile picture, even after you apply. Please do not type contact details into your CV text.</p>
<p>You can turn this off at any time. JobLink records when you turn it on or off, and each time a company opens your searchable profile.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">5. Required Clearances (NBI and Barangay)</h2>
<p>To apply for jobs, you must upload your NBI clearance and your barangay clearance as PDF files, each with the date it is valid until. By uploading them you agree that:</p>
<ul>
    <li>JobLink collects and stores them in private storage;</li>
    <li>every company you apply to can open them while your application to that company is active, and can no longer open them if you withdraw the application;</li>
    <li>the Job Coordinator, other companies and other students cannot open them, and they are not shown when companies search for candidates; and</li>
    <li>JobLink records when you upload, replace or remove a clearance, and each time a company opens one.</li>
</ul>
<p>You must upload only your own genuine clearances and enter the correct validity date. An expired clearance must be replaced before you can apply again. You can replace or remove a clearance at any time under My Clearances, and the old file is deleted. Companies may use a clearance only to assess your application, and may not copy it or share it with anyone else.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">6. Accuracy of Information</h2>
<p>You are responsible for keeping your contact and address details current.</p>
<p>Certain academic fields &mdash; full name, course/program, year level, section, and year graduated &mdash; are locked after your profile is completed and can only be corrected by your Job Coordinator in order to protect the integrity of official records.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">7. Account Security</h2>
<p>You are responsible for keeping your password confidential and for protecting access to your account.</p>
<p>If you suspect unauthorized access to your account, notify your Job Coordinator immediately.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">8. Acceptable Use</h2>
<p>When using JobLink, you agree not to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>post false or misleading job listings or applicant information;</li>
    <li>use contact details obtained through the platform from companies, applicants, or other users for purposes unrelated to legitimate recruitment;</li>
    <li>upload a clearance that is not yours, has been altered, or has a wrong validity date; or</li>
    <li>attempt to access accounts, records, or administrative functions that you are not authorized to use.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">9. Companies and Job Postings</h2>
<p>Companies are responsible for the accuracy of their job postings and for handling applicant data, including applicant profiles (CVs), clearances, contact information, and application status, in accordance with the applicable policies and laws.</p>
<p>Companies may use candidate search only to find people for real openings. They may not copy, export or share candidate profiles outside JobLink, try to find a candidate's hidden contact details, or use profiles for any other purpose. Each time a company opens a candidate profile, JobLink records it.</p>
<p>The Job Coordinator is responsible for reviewing job postings and may remove postings that violate these Terms &amp; Conditions.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">10. Data Retention and Removal</h2>
<p>The Job Coordinator may correct, update, or remove student and alumni records as needed for administrative accuracy.</p>
<p>You may contact your Job Coordinator to request information about the data associated with your account.</p>

<h2 class="h6" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
<p>These Terms &amp; Conditions may be updated from time to time.</p>
<p>Continued use of JobLink after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.</p>

<h2 class="h6 mb-2" style="color: var(--jl-navy);">12. Contact</h2>
<p class="mb-0">Questions about these Terms &amp; Conditions or your data should be directed to the Job Coordinator's office at PSU Alaminos City Campus.</p>
